      "worked": "If $f$ were odd, then for every $x\\ne\\pm k$,\n$$\\begin{align*}\n\\frac{-x-k}{-x+k}&=-\\frac{x-k}{x+k}\\\\\n(-x-k)(x+k)&=-(x-k)(-x+k)\\\\\n-(x+k)^2&=(x-k)^2\\\\\n0&=2x^2+2k^2\\\\\nx^2+k^2&=0.\n\\end{align*}$$\nFor nonzero $x\\ne\\pm k$, $x^2+k^2>0$, a contradiction. Hence no value of $k$ makes $f$ odd.",
